From: Try Roguix contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: leave Command-Tab to the macOS application switcher

Applies after the full-grab-focus and full-grab-reenable patches.

With Accessibility permission, full grab's HID event tap takes every Command
chord while the VM window is key, so Command-Tab becomes Super-Tab in the
guest and the keyboard can no longer leave the VM; only a trackpad swipe
does. Let Command-Tab and Command-Shift-Tab through the tap untouched, as
any other Mac app does. The guest has seen Command go down as Super; the
switch makes the window resign key, and windowDidResignKey releases it.

diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
index 4a8dd1d..0b97d4d 100644
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -429,6 +429,18 @@ static CGEventRef handleTapEvent(CGEventTapProxy proxy, CGEventType type, CGEven
         return cgEvent;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Command-Tab and Command-Shift-Tab stay with the macOS application
+     * switcher, as in a browser or any other app, so the user can always
+     * leave the VM from the keyboard. Switching away makes the window
+     * resign key, which releases the guest's Super key again.
+     */
+    if ((type == kCGEventKeyDown || type == kCGEventKeyUp) &&
+        CGEventGetIntegerValueField(cgEvent, kCGKeyboardEventKeycode) == kVK_Tab &&
+        (CGEventGetFlags(cgEvent) & kCGEventFlagMaskCommand)) {
+        return cgEvent;
+    }
+
     NSEvent *event = [NSEvent eventWithCGEvent:cgEvent];
     if ([view isKeyboardCaptured] && [view handleEvent:event]) {
         COCOA_DEBUG("Global events tap: qemu handled the event, capturing!\n");
